    "content": "Evidence review session 3 (invoice INV-2207): Line 1: 3 x 120 = 360. Line 2: 2 x 45 = 90. Sum of line items = 360 + 90 = 450. The invoice header states total due = 520. Therefore 520 does NOT equal the sum of the line items (450). The claim is factually incorrect based on the evidence on file. No challenger evidence has been posted yet."
  }'

curl -s -X POST "$VERACITY_URL/v1/episodes/case-13253a3d87a8-0003/forum/messages" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: juror1-evidence-review-0003-s3" \
  -d '{
    "content": "Evidence review session 3 (route 9 courier log): The delivery log records 12 parcels with delivery times: P-01 09:12, P-02 09:47, P-03 10:20, P-04 11:05, P-05 11:58, P-06 12:40, P-07 13:16, P-08 14:02, P-09 14:51, P-10 15:25, P-11 16:08, P-12 16:44. The deadline for every parcel is 17:00. All 12 delivery times are before 17:00; the latest is 16:44. Therefore the claim that all twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline is factually supported by the record. No challenger evidence has been posted yet."
  }'

curl -s -X POST "$VERACITY_URL/v1/episodes/case-13253a3d87a8-0004/forum/messages" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: juror1-evidence-review-0004-s3" \
  -d '{
    "content": "Evidence review session 3 (employee 4471 timesheet): The weekly timesheet records Monday 8, Tuesday 8, Wednesday 9, Thursday 7, Friday 8. Total hours = 8 + 8 + 9 + 7 + 8 = 40. No weekend shifts or overtime entries are recorded. The claim states 42 hours. Since 40 does not equal 42, the claim is factually incorrect based on the evidence on file. No challenger evidence has been posted yet."
  }'
